NOTICE

This repository quotes verbatim excerpts from Anthropic's public documentation,
articles and support pages, and one sentence from a public talk by an Anthropic
employee. The largest concentration is the prompt snippet
library in skill/*/references/snippets.md: 52 numbered entries, of which 51 are
verbatim excerpts (4.1 is a decision table, not a quotation), carrying 75
fenced blocks, 72 of them 40 characters or more, roughly 5,450 words, drawn
from nine documentation pages. The rest of the skill quotes roughly 755 further
words of official wording in fenced blocks -- 19 fenced blocks in all, roughly
925 words, the remainder being this repository's own skeletons -- and roughly
2,900 more inline, as shorter sentences, page headings and example prompts,
each counted once. The study guides quote roughly 2,200 more as individual
attributed sentences, each counted once across the two guides, which quote
largely the same English sentences. The Chinese edition of the skill translates
only this repository's own prose and templates and leaves every quoted block
byte-identical to the English edition's. That puts the total on the order of
11,000 words.

Those excerpts are the property of Anthropic. Each is attributed at the point of
use -- the snippet index links every quoted entry to its source page -- and in
SOURCES.md, and they are included for the purpose of documenting technique.

The MIT grant above covers this repository's own prose, structure, and tooling.
It does NOT cover the quoted material, and does not purport to grant anyone
rights to it.

This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Anthropic.
"Claude" and "Anthropic" are trademarks of Anthropic PBC and are used here only
descriptively, to identify the systems this material documents.
